          %p
            A
            %strong Markov category
            or
            %strong affine CD category
            is a CD category where any of these equivalent conditions hold:
          %ul
            %li
              The monoidal unit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              (i.e. the category is
              = succeed ");" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicartesian+monoidal+category"} semicartesian monoidal
            %li
              The discard (counit) maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi del
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} del:X\to I
              are part of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id\Rightarrow I
            %li
              For every morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi del
                        %mi Y
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} del
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} del_Y \circ f = \del_X
          %p The last equation can be written in terms of string diagrams as follows:
          %svg{:height => "53.8pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 99.596 53.8", :width => "99.596pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
