            %p
              In particular, every element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in Y
              can be seen as a
              %em constant
              function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
              which does not really depend on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p As we will see, once probabilities are involved, copying and discarding will require particular care, due to the presence of possible correlation. Markov and CD categories allow us to keep track of these operations graphically, avoiding many possible pitfalls, and even using them to our advantage.
          %h3#the_category_finstoch_of_stochastic_matrices
            The category
            %em FinStoch
            of stochastic matrices
          %p
            Let’s now look at a category where randomness is involved. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+matrix"} stochastic matrix
            = succeed "," do
