              %g{:style => "fill:rgb(0%,0%,0%);fill-opacity:1;"}
                %use{:x => "188.133963", "xlink:href" => "#92xf9cwDM0ETjYNBYfEnVtFDViI=-glyph3-1", :y => "49.788244"}
          %p
            A Markov category is said to
            %strong have conditionals
            if every conditional in the form above exists.
          %p
            Both
            %em FinStoch
            and
            %em BorelStoch
            have conditionals.
          %h2#further_structures_and_properties Further structures and properties
          %h3#representable_markov_categories Representable Markov categories
          %p
            %a{:href => "#kleisli_categories_of_probability_monads"}> As we explained above
            , a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monad"} probability monad
            often gives rise to a Markov category. We now characterize those that do, as representable Markov categories (Theorem
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#theorem:representable"}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#theorem:embed-in-representable"}
          %p
            Conversely, consider a Markov category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %ul
            %li
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi det
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_det
              of deterministic morphisms has no randomness;
            %li
              There may be have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi det
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\det
              which encodes randomness (see
              = succeed ");" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monad"} probability monad
            %li
              The Markov category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              may be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
              of this monad.
          %p
            Let’s make this precise in terms of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an object in a Markov category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong
              distribution object for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an object, which we denote by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
          #eq:adjunction.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi det
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C_det(A,P X) \cong C(A,X)
          %p
            for all objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            against deterministic morphisms.
          %p
            The object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            has the interpretation of being a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                space of probability measures over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A=I
            in the definition, we see in particular that the deterministic states (or “points”) of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            are exactly the (generic, random) states on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            should be exactly the probability measures on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
            every object has a distribution object, given by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
          %p More generally:
          %p
          #theorem:representable.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              For a Markov category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %ol
              %li
                Every object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has a distribution object.
              %li
                The inclusion functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi det
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_det\to C
                has a right adjoint (which we denote by
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is isomorphic to the Kleisli category of a commutative affine monad on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi det
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_det
            %p
          %p
            A Markov category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is called
            %strong representable
            if any of the conditions of the theorem above holds.
          %p
            The category
            %em FinStoch
            is not representable, since the objects are finite sets, and the set of distribution
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            over a finite set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (with more than two elements) would be infinite. It is however a subcategory of the Kleisli category of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution+monad"} distribution monad
            %em all sets
            and all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stochastic+maps"} stochastic maps
            between them.
          %p
            By means of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            together with a distinguished morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X\to X
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi samp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} samp
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sampling+map"} sampling map
            %svg{:height => "50.104pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 189.645 50.104", :width => "189.645pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
